rived to shut the ducks in.\" [577] \"Did you lock the door when you went out?\" [578] Miss Blacklock frowned. [579] \"I can't remember... I think I did. I'm sure I locked it when I came in.\" [580] \"It was just after a quarter to six then?\" [581] \"Something like that.\" [582] \"What about the front door?\" [583] \"It's usually locked later.\" [584] \"So Sherris could have easily come in through there, or he could have slipped in while you were shutting the ducks. He'd have had a good look at the layout, and he'd have noticed the hiding places - cupboards, that sort of thing. Yes, it all seems clear enough.\" [585] \"I beg your pardon, but there's still something I don't understand.\" Miss Blacklock said. \"Why on earth would anyone go to all this trouble to stage such a silly robbery?\" [586] \"You keep a lot of money at home, Miss Blacklock?\" [587] \"About five pounds in that drawer, and a couple of pounds in my purse.\" [588] \"What about jewelry?\" [589] \"One or two rings and a brooch, and the carved jade I'm wearing. You must agree with me, Inspector, the whole thing is absurd.\" [590] \"This was no ordinary break-in and robbery,\" Miss Bonner cried. \"I've been telling you so all along, Letty. This is revenge! Because you didn't give him the money! He deliberately shot at you \u2013 twice!\" [591] \"Ah,\" said Colonel Corcoran, \"let's talk about last night. What exactly happened, Miss Blacklock? Please tell me in your own words, as best you can remember.\" [592] Miss Blacklock paused for a moment. [593] \"The clock struck,\" she said. \"The one on the mantelpiece. I remember saying that if anything was going to happen, it would start right now. And then the clock struck. We all stood there in silence. It struck six-thirty, and suddenly, all the lights went out.\" [594] \"Which lights were on?\" [595] \"The lamps here and in the sitting room. The standard lamp and the two reading lamps weren't lit.\" [596] \"Did you see the flashlight first or hear a sound?\" [597] \"I'm not quite sure.\" [598] \"I'm certain it was the flashlight,\" said Dora Bunner, \"and then there was a creak. It was close.\" [599] \"And then, Miss Blacklock?\" [600] \"The door opened\u2014\"\n[601] \"Which one? There are two doors in this room.\" [602] \"Oh, this one. The other door won't open, it's just for show. The door opened, and out he came\u2014a man with a revolver in his left hand and a mask on his head. I was absolutely flabbergasted, of course, I thought it was just a silly joke. He said something\u2014I forget\u2014\"\n[603] \" 'Raise your hands, or I'll shoot!' \" Miss Bonner said dramatically. [604] \"Something like that,\" Miss Blacklock said doubtfully. [605] \"And then you both raised your hands?\" [606] \"Ah, yes,\" Miss Bonner said. \"We all raised our hands. I mean, it was part of the game.\" [607] \"I didn't,\" Miss Blacklock said firmly. \"It seemed ridiculous at the time. And I was quite annoyed with the whole thing.\" [608] \"Then what happened?\" [609] \"A flashlight beam shone right into my eyes, making me dizzy. Then, unbelievably, I heard a bullet whizz past my ear and hit the wall behind me. Someone screamed, and then I felt a searing pain in my ear and heard a second gunshot.\" [610] \"That was terrifying,\" Miss Bonner interjected. [611] \"What happened next, Miss Blacklock?\" [612] \"I'm not quite sure\u2014I was staggering around in pain and shock. The shadow turned around, stumbled, and then there was another gunshot. His flashlight went out, and everyone started pushing and shouting, all bumping into each other.\" [613] \"Where were you standing at the time, Miss Blacklock?\" [614] \"She was at the table. She was still holding the violet bottle.\" Miss Bonner panted. [615] \"I was right here,\" said Miss Blacklock, walking over to the small table by the arcade, \"still holding the cigarette box.\" [616] Inspector Corridor looked at the wall behind her, two bullet holes were clearly visible. The bullets had been