ld go out more often.) Sonya announced that she was going to marry a man named Dmitri Stanforth. I've only met him once. He's very attractive, but I must say, he's not to be relied upon. Randell strongly opposed him, calling him a scoundrel and a fraud. Bella, may the Lord bless her, just smiled and lay on the couch. Sonya, who had been expressionless, flew into a rage, ready to kill Randell. Yesterday, I thought she would! [2184] I've done my best. I talked to Sonya and to Randell, trying to get them to think rationally. When they got together, they started arguing again: you can't imagine how boring it was. Randell has been trying to find out more about Stanforth, and it seems that he's no good at all. [2185] Meanwhile, the business has been neglected. I've been working in the office, and in a way, it's been quite interesting because Randell has let me do it. Yesterday, he said to me, \"Thank God, there's at least one sane person in the world. You wouldn't fall in love with a scoundrel, would you, Blatch?\" I said I didn't think I would. Randell said, \"Let's discuss some of the minor issues in London.\" He can be a mischievous devil at times, and he can be hasty in a crisis. [2186] \"Are you determined to be an honest person, Blatch?\" he said one day. And I was indeed intending to be so! I cannot understand how people can ignore deceit, but Randall is really not clear-sighted. He only knows what is truly illegal. [2187] Bella just laughs at all this. She thinks that the whole Sonya affair is nonsense. \"Sonya has money of her own,\" she said, \"Why shouldn't she marry the man if she wants to?\" I said that this marriage would be a terrible mistake, and Bella said, \"Marriage to a man you love can never be a mistake \u2013 even if you regret it later.\" She also said, \"I think Sonya doesn't want to quarrel with Randall for the money. She really likes money.\" [2188] That's the situation now. How is your father? I will not say \"with regards\" to him. But if you 